# Calcium prelude
#
# Written in Calcium's own syntax, because a unit is nothing more than a
# definition and dimensional analysis is what falls out of ordinary symbolic
# algebra. `ft = 3048 m / 10000` is all it takes for `100 ft in m` to work.
#
# Names defined here are marked as units, which means they stay symbolic in
# ordinary expressions (so `4 weeks + 6 days` does not collapse into seconds)
# and expand only when an `in` conversion forces them to.
#
# SI magnitude prefixes are not enumerated; they are applied programmatically,
# so `PW`, `nW` and `µW` all work without appearing below.
#
# NOTE: two adjacent bare words are a single multi-word identifier in this
# language (`mass of earth`), so a product of units must be written with an
# explicit `*`. `N = kg m/s^2` would define N in terms of a variable literally
# named "kg m".

## Base units

m = m
kg = kg
s = s
A = A
K = K
mol = mol
cd = cd
rad = rad
bit = bit
$ = $

## Mathematical constants
#
# Constants, not units: they fold into arithmetic wherever they appear rather
# than staying symbolic until an `in` conversion.

#!constants

pi = 3.14159265358979323846264338327950288
π = pi
tau = 2*pi
e = 2.71828182845904523536028747135266250
phi = 1.61803398874989484820458683436563812

## Dimensionless

% = 1/100

#!units

