## Temperature
#
# These are the *sizes* of the degrees, which is all a definition can express:
# a Celsius degree is a kelvin, a Fahrenheit degree is five ninths of one. That
# makes `J/degC` correctly equal to `J/K`, and a difference of temperatures
# come out right.
#
# Where they measure *from* is not expressible here — there is nowhere in a
# multiplication to put an addition — so the zero point lives in the engine and
# is applied by `in`. See AFFINE_UNITS in eval.rs.

kelvin = K
kelvins = K
degC = K
celsius = degC
degF = 5 K/9
fahrenheit = degF
degR = 5 K/9
rankine = degR

